{ id: "ARC-M02", subject: "Maths", topicKey: "areas-related-to-circles", subtopic: "Composite Figures", section: "C", marks: 3, format: "Short", difficulty: "Medium", bloomSkill: "Applying", questionText: "A round table cover has six equal designs as shown in figure. If the radius of the cover is 28 cm, find the cost of making the designs at the rate of ₹0.35 per cm². (Use √3 = 1.7)", solutionSteps: [
      "The cover is divided into 6 equilateral triangles by radii; Central angle per sector = 60°; Area of each sector = (60/360) × (22/7) × 28² = (1/6) × 2464 = 410.67 cm² [1]",
      "Area of equilateral triangle = (√3/4) × 28² = (1.7/4) × 784 = 333.2 cm²; Area of each design (segment) = 410.67 − 333.2 = 77.47 cm² [1]",
      "Total area of 6 designs = 6 × 77.47 = 464.8 cm²; Cost = 464.8 × 0.35 = ₹162.68 [1]",
    ], finalAnswer: "≈ ₹162.68" , isCompetencyBased: true }

{ id: "ARC-M06", subject: "Maths", topicKey: "areas-related-to-circles", subtopic: "Composite Figures", section: "C", marks: 3, format: "Short", difficulty: "Medium", bloomSkill: "Applying", questionText: "A round table cover has six equal designs as shown. If the radius of the cover is 28 cm, find the cost of making the designs at the rate of ₹0.35 per cm². (Use √3 = 1.7)", solutionSteps: [
      "6 designs = 6 segments, each with central angle 60°; Area of each segment = sector − equilateral triangle part; Sector area = (60/360) × 22/7 × 784 = 410.67 cm² [1]",
      "Triangle area = (√3/4) × 28² = (1.7/4) × 784 = 333.2 cm²; Each segment = 77.47 cm² [1]",
      "6 segments = 464.8 cm²; Cost = 464.8 × 0.35 = ₹162.68 [1]",
    ], finalAnswer: "≈ ₹162.68" , isCompetencyBased: true }

{ id: "CIR-M08", subject: "Maths", topicKey: "circles", subtopic: "Tangent Properties", section: "B", marks: 2, format: "Short", difficulty: "Medium", bloomSkill: "Applying", questionText: "A quadrilateral ABCD is drawn to circumscribe a circle. Prove that AB + CD = AD + BC.", solutionSteps: [
      "Construction: Draw a circle with centre O and mark the point of tangency. Draw the tangent line at that point.; Let tangent lengths: AP = AS = a, BP = BQ = b, CQ = CR = c, DR = DS = d [½]",
      "AB + CD = (a+b) + (c+d); AD + BC = (a+d) + (b+c) [½]",
      "Both equal a + b + c + d [1]",
    ], finalAnswer: "AB + CD = AD + BC (proved)" , visualExplainerId: "maths-circles-tangent-to-a-circle", isCompetencyBased: true }

{ id: "CIR-M05", subject: "Maths", topicKey: "circles", subtopic: "Tangent Properties", section: "C", marks: 3, format: "Short", difficulty: "Medium", bloomSkill: "Applying", questionText: "In the figure, XY and X'Y' are two parallel tangents to a circle with centre O and another tangent AB with point of contact C intersects XY at A and X'Y' at B. Prove that ∠AOB = 90°.", solutionSteps: [
      "Construction: Draw a circle with centre O and mark the point of tangency. Draw the tangent line at that point.; Join OC. In △OPA and △OCA: OP = OC (radii), OA common, PA = CA (tangents) [1]",
      "△OPA ≅ △OCA (SSS). So ∠POA = ∠COA; Similarly ∠QOB = ∠COB [1]",
      "∠POA + ∠COA + ∠COB + ∠QOB = 180° (POQ is straight line); 2∠COA + 2∠COB = 180° → ∠AOB = 90° [1]",
    ], finalAnswer: "∠AOB = 90° (proved)" , visualExplainerId: "maths-circles-tangent-to-a-circle", isCompetencyBased: true }

{ id: "CG-M19", subject: "Maths", topicKey: "coordinate-geometry", subtopic: "Distance Formula", section: "C", marks: 3, format: "Short", difficulty: "Medium", bloomSkill: "Applying", questionText: "If the distances of P(x, y) from A(5, 1) and B(−1, 5) are equal, find 3x = 2y.", solutionSteps: [
      "(x−5)²+(y−1)² = (x+1)²+(y−5)² [1]",
      "−10x+25−2y+1 = 2x+1−10y+25 [1]",
      "−12x+8y = 0 → 3x = 2y [1]",
    ], finalAnswer: "3x = 2y (proved)" , isCompetencyBased: true }

